1
00:02:07,510 --> 00:02:10,240
- What did you say your name was again?
- Sean.

2
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:13,720
Sean, yeah. I did business
with a guy named Sean once.

3
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:17,650
- Fucked me over real good.
- Well, you can trust me, sir.

4
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:21,660
This woman wants her car delivered
by Tuesday. That's five days from now.

5
00:02:21,730 --> 00:02:25,420
- Okay, I can do it. I worked out...
- I don't give a shit how you do it...

6
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:28,290
so long as it gets there by Tuesday
and in one piece.

7
00:02:28,370 --> 00:02:30,360
And if it doesn't,
that bitch is gonna ream my ass.

8
00:02:30,430 --> 00:02:32,770
If that happens,
I'm gonna come looking for yours.

9
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:35,170
- Yes, sir.
- What the hell are you eating?

10
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:37,830
- None of your goddamn business.
- What did the doctor say?

11
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:40,000
Oh, fuck the doctor.
You got them papers yet?

12
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:42,570
- I'm getting there.
- Been getting there for the last hour.

13
00:02:42,650 --> 00:02:45,670
I'm getting there, Ned,
and I'm still getting there.

14
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:47,880
These are your papers
and your registration.

15
00:02:47,950 --> 00:02:50,040
They'll explain everything
if the cops pull you over.

16
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:52,320
- But that ain't gonna happen.
- No, sir.

17
00:02:52,390 --> 00:02:54,650
This one's our contract.
You get half your fee up front.

18
00:02:54,730 --> 00:02:57,220
And the other half
when you deliver the car.

19
00:02:57,290 --> 00:02:59,350
Here. Sign here.

20
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,860
What about insurance?

21
00:03:02,930 --> 00:03:04,730
Don't worry. I'm covered.

22
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,360
If you get into an accident
and it's the other guy's fault...

23
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:09,700
just call me.

24
00:03:09,770 --> 00:03:11,640
What if it's my fault?

25
00:03:11,710 --> 00:03:14,870
Well, then you'd better hope to hell
I never catch your ass.

26
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:23,150
Now remember.
This ain't no sightseeing trip.

27
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:25,850
If you fuck around,
you're not gonna make Miami by Tuesday.

28
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:29,480
And no goddamn hitchhikers.

29
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:32,320
I don't care what kind of hard-luck
story they give. Don't pick them up.

30
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:36,090
It's just asking for trouble.
Woman's a real ball-buster.

31
00:03:36,170 --> 00:03:39,160
Her husband ran off
with some Florida State cheerleader...

32
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:41,500
and she got this beauty
in the divorce settlement.

33
00:03:41,570 --> 00:03:45,440
- And she doesn't want a scratch on it.
- Sure this thing will make it to Miami?

34
00:03:45,510 --> 00:03:48,310
Not that old piece of shit.
This one.

35
00:04:07,870 --> 00:04:12,100
- You should have seen this guy.
- A $50,000 car.

36
00:04:12,170 --> 00:04:14,540
Absolutely primo.
The husband restored everything...

37
00:04:14,610 --> 00:04:17,130
right down to the nuts and bolts.

38
00:04:17,210 --> 00:04:20,110
Well, when are you splitting?

39
00:04:20,180 --> 00:04:22,200
As soon as I tell Decker.

40
00:04:23,450 --> 00:04:27,040
He's never gonna let you go,
not in a million years.

41
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,880
The geek wants to see you
in his office, Sean.

42
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,830
Saw the car, dude. It's dope.

43
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:42,660
- He's gonna get fired.
- Decker wouldn't dare. Sean rules.

44
00:04:42,730 --> 00:04:45,400
- I'll bet you ten bucks he gets canned.
- You're on.

45
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:52,900
- You wanted to see me?
- What's this about taking the week off?

46
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:57,640
My sister's getting married. I thought
I couldn't go. I didn't have the bucks...

47
00:04:57,710 --> 00:05:00,910
- What's Teen Zombie's release date?
- September 1 5.

48
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:04,440
- I got to deliver a trailer by August.
- I can mix and deliver in time.

49
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:07,320
- I got a week's vacation coming.
- You don't see me taking a vacation.

50
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:10,850
If I went around all the time,
this place would go to shit.

51
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:16,100
All right. You want to fire me,
fine, but I'm going.

52
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:20,630
One week. That's it. And if that trailer
isn't on time, your ass is out of here.

53
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:22,540
- Thanks.
- Fuck you.

54
00:05:24,810 --> 00:05:26,240
So?

55
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:33,350
I'll see you guys in a week.

56
00:06:30,170 --> 00:06:33,340
- Hey, where you headed, cowboy?
- Miami.

57
00:06:33,410 --> 00:06:35,570
We're going to Big Bob Dune Races.

58
00:06:35,650 --> 00:06:37,610
It's on your way.
You should check it out.

59
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:40,340
- I can't.
- Aw, why not?

60
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:42,410
I got kind of a tight schedule.

61
00:06:42,490 --> 00:06:46,250
You know, it's too bad 'cause
you don't know what you're missing.

62
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:48,050
Holy shit!

63
00:07:34,670 --> 00:07:35,600
Fuck!

64
00:07:44,150 --> 00:07:47,450
Ain't not damage except to the rim,
as far as I can tell.

65
00:07:49,250 --> 00:07:52,150
I could pound it out for you
to make it look as good as new.

66
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:55,160
It would take me till tomorrow
to get that size of tire.

67
00:07:55,230 --> 00:07:56,850
What about using the spare?

68
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,330
The highway's shut down up ahead
for the next 30 miles.

69
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:05,060
You gotta take some back roads.

70
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:08,000
I wouldn't want to get caught
out in the badlands without a spare.

71
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:13,640
Yeah, this is great. I lost my wallet.
I can't believe this.

72
00:08:13,710 --> 00:08:18,670
- You gonna be able to pay for this?
- Yeah. Yeah, sure.

73
00:08:18,750 --> 00:08:21,110
I was saving this
for my sister's wedding present.

74
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:25,350
Yeah. Yeah,
I can pay for the tire.

75
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:29,450
Hey, this motel down here...
is it clean?

76
00:08:29,530 --> 00:08:31,960
Huh?

77
00:08:44,340 --> 00:08:47,500
Fourteen. How was it?

78
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:55,110
Now what good is all that?

79
00:08:55,190 --> 00:08:57,710
You know, he's only
gonna come back with the others.

80
00:09:00,190 --> 00:09:02,750
- And you'll get shot.
- We're gonna get you out so fast...

81
00:09:02,830 --> 00:09:04,760
you won't touch ground.

82
00:09:10,670 --> 00:09:13,930
Wait a minute. I helped you out
this far. Now I'm finished.

83
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,270
- You're what?
- I said I'm finished.

84
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:18,740
I come into town on business.

85
00:09:18,810 --> 00:09:20,970
Look, my cattle's dying.
I gotta take care of them.

86
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:24,610
- Dan, you're the best shot we've got.
- Well, that's not my job.

87
00:12:00,370 --> 00:12:01,390
Thanks.

88
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:17,350
Nice ride. Where you headed?

89
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:22,060
Florida.

90
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:27,920
- You going through Houston?
- Yeah.

91
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,090
Well, I'm pointed that way.

92
00:12:30,170 --> 00:12:32,930
What are the chances
of you giving me a lift?

93
00:12:34,340 --> 00:12:36,770
Come on, man.
It's a long, lonely ride by yourself.

94
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:39,000
You could use some company, huh?

95
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:42,010
Look, man, I'm sorry.
It's not my car, all right?

96
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:45,280
I'm driving it for the owner.
Part of the deal is no hitchhikers.

97
00:12:45,350 --> 00:12:47,510
The sun's killing me.

98
00:12:47,580 --> 00:12:49,710
The local dick...
he's already stopped me twice.

99
00:12:49,790 --> 00:12:53,310
- Asked me to get my ass out of town.
- You'll get a ride.

100
00:12:53,390 --> 00:12:55,220
What if I don't?

101
00:12:57,130 --> 00:12:59,250
What if you pick up the newspaper
tomorrow and you read about...

102
00:12:59,330 --> 00:13:02,560
some slacker road kill with a picture
of my face staring back at you, huh?

103
00:13:02,630 --> 00:13:05,690
Could you live with that?

104
00:13:05,770 --> 00:13:07,900
I'll pay for gas!

105
00:13:21,020 --> 00:13:22,950
All the gas until Houston?

106
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:24,950
Name's Nick.

107
00:13:25,020 --> 00:13:27,050
Sean.

108
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:29,060
You made the right decision, Sean.

109
00:13:39,070 --> 00:13:41,540
My sister kept everything together
after my mom died.

110
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:44,470
Went to work out of high school.
Put herself through college.

111
00:13:44,540 --> 00:13:46,700
Put me through film school.

112
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:48,710
I really wanna be there
for her wedding.

113
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:50,710
You make a lot of money
in the movie biz?

114
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:53,510
Not yet.
Right now I'm just cutting trailers.

115
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:58,140
- What are trailers?
- You know, coming attractions.

116
00:13:58,220 --> 00:14:00,450
I cut the video trailers
for Death Ball and Sorority Killers.

117
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:02,820
Really?

118
00:14:02,890 --> 00:14:05,290
Well, can't say I saw those.

119
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:08,060
Movies are at the bottom
of the entertainment food chain for me.

120
00:14:08,130 --> 00:14:11,860
No, I wanna cut features.
That is where the real money is.

121
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:14,130
Maybe direct someday.

122
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:16,400
My dad was the second assistant on E. T.

123
00:14:17,470 --> 00:14:19,410
Now I saw that one.

124
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:22,570
Me and my friend scored some killer bud
one night, and we rented it.

125
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:33,560
What are you doing?

126
00:14:34,690 --> 00:14:37,490
Drinking a beer.
Only one left, and it's warm.

127
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:39,990
- If you say please, I'll share it.
- Not while I'm driving.

128
00:14:41,430 --> 00:14:42,860
That's cool.

129
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,430
I mean both of us.

130
00:14:48,070 --> 00:14:51,170
- I'm not driving.
- I don't wanna chance getting busted.

131
00:14:52,540 --> 00:14:55,910
Who the hell is gonna bust us out here?
I haven't even seen any road kill.

132
00:14:55,980 --> 00:14:58,950
That's not the point. Besides,
I don't want you spilling it in the car.

133
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:01,580
- I'm not a fucking geek!
- Listen, get rid of it.

134
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:30,380
You said get rid of it.

135
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:50,490
- Still pissed? You don't have to pay.
- You ever hear of a warrant?

136
00:15:50,570 --> 00:15:52,500
You don't even live in this state.

137
00:15:52,570 --> 00:15:55,270
I mean, unless you're worried
about being extradited for littering.

138
00:15:55,340 --> 00:15:57,700
He didn't even bust you
for the open container.

139
00:15:57,770 --> 00:16:00,240
Hey, don't push it, all right?

140
00:16:04,610 --> 00:16:06,780
Hey, man, you gotta lighten up.

141
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:15,690
How you boys doing this evening?

142
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:18,660
Fine. You?

143
00:16:18,730 --> 00:16:22,100
Son of a bitch died on us just
as we pulled in here to take a piss.

144
00:16:22,170 --> 00:16:26,260
- Think the battery's gone dead.
- We need a jump.

145
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:30,970
- I don't have any cables.
- That's okay. We got some.

146
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:33,300
So, what do you say?

147
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:36,110
Yeah, sure. Let's do it.

148
00:16:37,180 --> 00:16:40,310
You want to pop the hood?

149
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:42,750
Get in and turn it over
when I tell you.

150
00:16:47,690 --> 00:16:50,220
We really appreciate your help.

151
00:16:50,290 --> 00:16:52,850
Thank you.
I'd sure hate to get stuck out here...

152
00:16:52,930 --> 00:16:54,990
in this shit-hole.

153
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:58,430
Hey, how much you pay
for a ride like that?

154
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:01,990
- I don't know. It's not mine.
- Well, whose is it?

155
00:17:02,070 --> 00:17:05,340
Shut up, Pen.
Kick it over, Teddy.

156
00:17:06,710 --> 00:17:07,870
Fuck.

157
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:14,220
Again.

158
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:19,550
Fuckin' A. Ready?

159
00:17:21,890 --> 00:17:25,160
You might want to keep that running
for a while. Let it charge up.

160
00:17:25,230 --> 00:17:26,660
We'll do that.

161
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:37,860
Can I ask you guys,
were you in Tonopah last night?

162
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:42,200
We were in Kingman last night.

163
00:17:43,780 --> 00:17:47,010
I thought I saw your car
in the motel there.

164
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:49,750
No, must have been another one
just like it.

165
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:52,580
Yeah, yeah. I guess so.

166
00:18:02,530 --> 00:18:05,000
You got any money you could spare?

167
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:09,570
- Not really.
- You sure?

168
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:11,870
Don't be a bitch. You heard him.

169
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:15,480
No harm in asking, right?

170
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:30,350
- The one riding shotgun's a hunter.
- I know.

171
00:18:30,430 --> 00:18:33,690
Then why did you let him go?

172
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:35,960
How many times
do I have to tell you?

173
00:18:36,030 --> 00:18:39,090
There's a time and a place...

174
00:18:39,170 --> 00:18:40,600
for everything.

175
00:18:58,050 --> 00:19:00,080
How's that steak?

176
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,680
It's good. Want some?

177
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:04,060
- You sure?
- Yeah.

178
00:19:04,130 --> 00:19:06,220
If that was any rarer,
it'd still be grazing somewhere.

179
00:19:08,930 --> 00:19:11,530
Do you eat like that
'cause you're tapped out?

180
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:15,230
Yeah, I'm tapped out. Lost my wallet,
credit cards, everything.

181
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:17,740
Got barely enough money
to get to my sister's wedding and back.

182
00:19:17,810 --> 00:19:19,240
Fucking ordered cheese.

183
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,740
So what's your deal, man?
What do you do?

184
00:19:26,820 --> 00:19:28,410
As little as possible.

185
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:31,510
Yeah, but you gotta make money.
You work?

186
00:19:32,290 --> 00:19:34,850
I cruise.
I find something to do when I need to.

187
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:37,050
Kind of like a day-to-day thing.

188
00:19:37,130 --> 00:19:39,060
What about the future?

189
00:19:39,130 --> 00:19:43,030
I mean, what do you want to be doing,
say, I don't know, ten years from now?

190
00:19:43,900 --> 00:19:46,300
I don't give a shit.
I could be dead tomorrow.

191
00:19:47,570 --> 00:19:49,940
If everybody had your attitude,
we'd really be fucked.

192
00:19:50,010 --> 00:19:53,970
We are fucked. Take a look
at the world we inherited.

193
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:57,570
We're a bunch of fast-food munching
MTV freaks humping the American dream.

194
00:19:58,750 --> 00:20:00,770
You gonna finish that pie?

195
00:20:02,350 --> 00:20:05,080
No. No, I guess I'm not.

196
00:20:05,150 --> 00:20:08,650
The generation before us sold their
innocence for 200 satellite stations...

197
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:10,660
and it's been downhill ever since.

198
00:20:10,730 --> 00:20:14,560
They had Mickey Mouse,
Easy Rider and the Beatles.

199
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:17,760
All right? We got South Park,
the Blair bitch and Ricky Martin.

200
00:20:17,830 --> 00:20:21,070
They had, "Be here now."
We got, "Shit happens."

201
00:20:21,140 --> 00:20:24,160
If that doesn't put things into
perspective, I don't know what does.

202
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:27,300
We're just Microsoft Neanderthals
addicted to surfing Net land...

203
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:29,310
still shitting in our own nest.

204
00:20:29,380 --> 00:20:32,250
And every time I think about giving
a rat's ass, I just picture Monica...

205
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:34,580
making millions
from sucking Bill's little red rooster.

206
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:37,920
And that just rockets me
right back into reality.

207
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:42,650
You are really depressing.
You know that, right?

208
00:20:42,730 --> 00:20:43,820
Yes.

209
00:20:43,890 --> 00:20:46,730
Here. My treat.

210
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:49,290
You pay. I'm gonna piss.

211
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:42,480
Look, miss.
This is a private tour bus.

212
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:45,440
I don't know what's wrong with you,
but if you wanna go somewhere...

213
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:48,490
you gotta get inside and buy yourself
a ticket for the regular bus.

214
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:59,930
You owe me for the coffee, honey.

215
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,700
- What's wrong with you?
- What's going on?

216
00:22:04,040 --> 00:22:06,200
- I don't know.
- What is wrong with her?

217
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:08,870
I think she's stoned
and flat-ass broke too.

218
00:22:08,950 --> 00:22:11,880
That's great.
Who's gonna pay me for this?

219
00:22:12,780 --> 00:22:14,580
I will.

220
00:22:16,350 --> 00:22:18,010
- I'll pay.
- If she's a friend...

221
00:22:18,090 --> 00:22:20,890
you better get her some help
before the sheriff sees her around here.

222
00:22:22,790 --> 00:22:24,620
It's okay.

223
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:28,930
I know what's wrong with you,
and I wanna help you.

224
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:31,760
- Easy, Nick. You're scaring her.
- I know what I'm doing, Sean.

225
00:22:31,830 --> 00:22:34,930
- I'm serious. Take it easy.
- I said I know what I'm doing.

226
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:37,940
Hey, look at her. She's shaking.

227
00:22:38,010 --> 00:22:41,070
- Get the car.
- Look, I can't get involved in this.

228
00:22:41,140 --> 00:22:42,770
Get the fucking car!

229
00:22:42,850 --> 00:22:44,280
Fuck!

230
00:22:53,860 --> 00:22:57,020
Well, I can let you have number six.

231
00:22:57,090 --> 00:22:59,620
It's 45 bucks.

232
00:22:59,700 --> 00:23:02,630
- Yeah, that's fine.
- In advance.

233
00:23:03,730 --> 00:23:06,630
I'm tired of you dune racers
fucking the place up...

234
00:23:06,700 --> 00:23:10,160
so no funny business
or I'll boot your ass out.

235
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:12,640
- Understood?
- Yes, sir.

236
00:23:15,140 --> 00:23:18,080
She was trying to get on that bus. Maybe
wherever it's going is where she's from.

237
