00:46:40,950 --> 00:46:44,510
Wanna get to know her better?
Catch a movie with her?

481
00:46:44,590 --> 00:46:47,150
Just make sure you keep her away
from any major arteries.

482
00:46:47,220 --> 00:46:50,710
- That's not funny.
- Exactly.

483
00:46:56,300 --> 00:46:57,590
It just doesn't seem fair.

484
00:46:58,970 --> 00:47:00,870
What's that?

485
00:47:03,170 --> 00:47:06,370
I wanna put her on the pills.
Let me become the decoy.

486
00:47:08,940 --> 00:47:11,910
She was bitten way before me. That means
I've got longer before I turn.

487
00:47:11,980 --> 00:47:14,140
- I don't care. I said no.
- Why?

488
00:47:14,220 --> 00:47:17,550
Because when the time comes,
I'm gonna need all the muscle I can get.

489
00:47:19,590 --> 00:47:22,250
What is going on with this guy?

490
00:47:23,520 --> 00:47:24,820
Jesus.

491
00:47:27,730 --> 00:47:30,960
There's another lane, asshole! Fuck.

492
00:47:37,570 --> 00:47:39,300
This guy's seriously psycho.

493
00:47:43,080 --> 00:47:45,840
- Fuck, it's them!
- What? Oh, great.

494
00:47:45,910 --> 00:47:47,900
What do we do now?

495
00:47:52,690 --> 00:47:56,320
- Control her!
- I'm trying to!

496
00:47:57,190 --> 00:48:00,320
- Can you go faster?
- Yeah, I can drive faster.

497
00:48:00,390 --> 00:48:02,790
Then do it! Drive faster!
Let's get the hell out of here!

498
00:48:04,830 --> 00:48:07,460
- You ain't going fast!
- I can't!

499
00:48:09,240 --> 00:48:11,970
- Shit!
- Oh, shit!

500
00:48:14,410 --> 00:48:16,600
He shot the son of a bitch's car!

501
00:48:25,450 --> 00:48:27,480
Get in the back seat!

502
00:48:33,160 --> 00:48:35,030
You bite me, I'll kill you!

503
00:48:36,430 --> 00:48:38,460
- Hang on.
- What are you doing?

504
00:48:38,530 --> 00:48:40,500
- I got an idea.
- Is it a good one?

505
00:48:40,570 --> 00:48:43,200
I don't know.
I'm about to find out.

506
00:49:07,030 --> 00:49:08,690
Shit!

507
00:49:12,170 --> 00:49:15,360
- Fucking skank! Look at the car!
- Who cares? Get in the car!

508
00:49:15,440 --> 00:49:17,370
We don't have time for this!

509
00:49:18,440 --> 00:49:20,600
Don't let her get away!

510
00:49:21,810 --> 00:49:24,180
Come here! Stop it!

511
00:49:24,250 --> 00:49:27,240
- Stop it!
- Hold her.

512
00:49:27,320 --> 00:49:29,440
- No. They already know where we are!
- Come on!

513
00:49:29,520 --> 00:49:33,010
Listen to me. Either she gets
on the cocktail, or I stop taking it.

514
00:49:33,090 --> 00:49:35,350
And no more morphine,
or she'll never talk.

515
00:49:36,860 --> 00:49:38,830
Shit! What the fuck
did you do that for?

516
00:49:38,890 --> 00:49:41,290
No more time for these games!
We gotta get to the mission!

517
00:49:41,360 --> 00:49:44,260
Come on!

518
00:49:44,330 --> 00:49:45,890
Let's go! Come on!

519
00:50:05,690 --> 00:50:07,050
Get down!

520
00:50:08,720 --> 00:50:11,490
- Go!
- Shit!

521
00:50:12,360 --> 00:50:15,490
You gotta be fucking kidding me!
Fuck!

522
00:50:15,560 --> 00:50:17,830
Son of a bitch died on us again!

523
00:50:17,900 --> 00:50:19,830
Why the fuck can't you keep
this car running?

524
00:50:19,900 --> 00:50:22,560
You shut your fucking face!
It's not my fault!

525
00:50:28,140 --> 00:50:30,170
Why aren't they following us, Nick?

526
00:50:31,750 --> 00:50:33,180
I don't know.

527
00:50:40,250 --> 00:50:41,740
Shit.

528
00:50:41,820 --> 00:50:45,310
It's not my fault they don't put
any money in the damn car.

529
00:50:45,390 --> 00:50:47,950
Keep wasting it on that bitch.

530
00:50:48,030 --> 00:50:51,330
Maybe if you put some money
in the car...

531
00:50:51,400 --> 00:50:53,330
we wouldn't be here, would we?

532
00:51:11,120 --> 00:51:12,550
Fucking whore.

533
00:51:18,060 --> 00:51:19,990
Oh, boy.

534
00:51:25,470 --> 00:51:28,490
Hey, we got one.

535
00:51:30,270 --> 00:51:33,970
- You want some of this shit?
- Yeah. Right here.

536
00:51:35,040 --> 00:51:37,600
- Geez, look. Check her out, man. Look.
- Ah, man!

537
00:51:37,680 --> 00:51:39,700
- Oh, man.
- Oh, man.

538
00:51:39,780 --> 00:51:41,810
- Pussy!
- Pussy!

539
00:51:53,690 --> 00:51:56,890
- What's up, sugar?
- Car died. I don't know what happened.

540
00:51:56,960 --> 00:52:00,900
This retard here can't seem
to keep the goddamn thing going.

541
00:52:00,970 --> 00:52:02,060
Shut up.

542
00:52:04,410 --> 00:52:08,100
So, what do you think?

543
00:52:09,840 --> 00:52:11,470
Can you help us out?

544
00:52:13,380 --> 00:52:14,940
We could take a look.

545
00:52:15,020 --> 00:52:17,580
Great. We're lucky you came along.

546
00:52:17,650 --> 00:52:19,640
Most people wouldn't stop out here
at night.

547
00:52:19,720 --> 00:52:24,660
Yeah. We really appreciate your help.

548
00:52:26,090 --> 00:52:28,930
- I'll get the tools.
- All right, then.

549
00:52:39,440 --> 00:52:40,840
Give her more pills.

550
00:52:40,910 --> 00:52:43,840
- If I give her any more, she'll O.D.
- Why is she still fucked up?

551
00:52:43,910 --> 00:52:46,810
The cocktail works slower
when you're closer to turning, Sean.

552
00:52:48,480 --> 00:52:50,880
- What's the matter?
- We're running out of gas.

553
00:52:50,950 --> 00:52:54,720
- How can we be running out of gas?
- Because they hit the tank.

554
00:52:54,790 --> 00:52:57,660
- How much we got left?
- I don't know. Ten or fifteen miles.

555
00:52:57,730 --> 00:53:01,790
- What do I look like, a mechanic?
- That's excellent.

556
00:53:01,860 --> 00:53:06,200
I'm gonna check out this shed.
You stay with her, all right?

557
00:53:54,980 --> 00:53:56,920
- Hey.
- Jesus!

558
00:53:58,550 --> 00:54:01,890
- Is that what I think it is?
- I told you to stay in the car.

559
00:54:01,960 --> 00:54:03,890
I heard a noise. I got worried.

560
00:54:06,360 --> 00:54:08,120
That's the car.

561
00:54:10,870 --> 00:54:13,890
- Hurry up. We gotta stop her! The car!
- I'm moving!

562
00:54:13,970 --> 00:54:16,100
Run! Stop!

563
00:54:16,170 --> 00:54:19,570
Wait! Stop the car!

564
00:54:19,640 --> 00:54:23,440
I got all my shit in there!
Come on!

565
00:54:26,410 --> 00:54:27,850
Damn!

566
00:55:13,290 --> 00:55:15,890
Yeah, by the looks of it,
you're probably gonna need...

567
00:55:15,960 --> 00:55:19,830
- Oh, what the fuck?
- Let's take a walk.

568
00:55:19,900 --> 00:55:22,870
- What's going on?
- Time to die, cowboy.

569
00:55:29,540 --> 00:55:32,540
I got 40 bucks on me.
That's all I got.

570
00:55:32,610 --> 00:55:34,550
But I got credit cards.
I can give you the PI N number.

571
00:55:34,620 --> 00:55:37,050
This is far enough.

572
00:55:37,120 --> 00:55:40,050
- Kneel down.
- Just take the wallet, please.

573
00:55:40,120 --> 00:55:41,640
Kneel down.

574
00:55:53,130 --> 00:55:55,660
- Girlfriend?
- Yeah, she's my girlfriend.

575
00:55:55,740 --> 00:55:58,930
And we're thinking about getting married
after we graduate.

576
00:55:59,010 --> 00:56:02,970
And her dad is so rich.
And I could call him.

577
00:56:03,040 --> 00:56:05,770
And he's got so much money...

578
00:56:07,410 --> 00:56:09,350
Please, God, don't do this to me.

579
00:56:18,390 --> 00:56:21,090
Got your whole life planned out,
do you?

580
00:56:42,920 --> 00:56:44,850
What you want me to do
with their car?

581
00:56:44,920 --> 00:56:46,750
We're taking it.

582
00:56:55,630 --> 00:56:58,430
You know how long
I've been tracking this guy for?

583
00:56:59,730 --> 00:57:01,170
Nine months.

584
00:57:02,940 --> 00:57:05,030
It's not easy.
They hide their killing.

585
00:57:05,110 --> 00:57:07,670
Make it look like a gang fight.

586
00:57:07,740 --> 00:57:11,010
Robberies. A guy riding a freight train
killing old women.

587
00:57:11,080 --> 00:57:13,270
All kinds of shit.
Almost all serial killers.

588
00:57:16,050 --> 00:57:18,280
Here. Let me get this.

589
00:57:20,320 --> 00:57:21,750
It's weird.

590
00:57:23,590 --> 00:57:27,750
Three days ago, I had a phat job
and not a worry in the world.

591
00:57:27,830 --> 00:57:30,390
And now I'm gonna turn
into a vampire...

592
00:57:30,460 --> 00:57:34,260
if I don't whack
some freaked-out psycho.

593
00:57:36,500 --> 00:57:38,440
On top of all that,
I'm gonna lose my job.

594
00:57:42,380 --> 00:57:45,780
How'd you get into the movie biz
anyways? Your old man?

595
00:57:48,120 --> 00:57:50,170
My old man doesn't know I exist.

596
00:57:53,920 --> 00:57:57,450
Yeah. He walked out on my mom
when she was pregnant with me.

597
00:57:59,860 --> 00:58:02,920
- That's fucked up.
- Yeah.

598
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:07,260
I guess it just must be
in the blood then, huh?

599
00:58:07,330 --> 00:58:09,000
Like father, like son.

600
00:58:10,240 --> 00:58:12,260
Shit, I hope not.

601
00:58:12,340 --> 00:58:14,740
My mom told me my dad was
a cross-dressing Marine drill sergeant.

602
00:58:30,660 --> 00:58:32,960
Where did you get this?

603
00:58:33,030 --> 00:58:36,550
I found it along the road
while I was hitching.

604
00:58:36,630 --> 00:58:38,560
You gotta be pretty pissed, huh?

605
00:58:38,630 --> 00:58:40,860
You had my fucking wallet
the whole time?

606
00:58:40,930 --> 00:58:42,530
Yeah.

607
00:58:42,600 --> 00:58:46,660
- And you didn't tell me?
- No.

608
00:58:50,180 --> 00:58:52,740
That's fucked up.

609
00:58:57,320 --> 00:58:58,250
There it is.

610
00:59:06,330 --> 00:59:09,420
This car's trashed, man.

611
00:59:09,500 --> 00:59:13,430
Do you know how much a new transmission
in a car like this is gonna cost?

612
00:59:13,500 --> 00:59:15,590
Would you stop worrying about the car?

613
00:59:15,670 --> 00:59:17,360
Is that her?

614
00:59:35,820 --> 00:59:38,150
Let me handle this.

615
00:59:40,530 --> 00:59:42,460
It's okay. Come on.
Now listen to me.

616
00:59:42,530 --> 00:59:44,930
We are the only ones
who can get you out of this alive.

617
00:59:45,000 --> 00:59:46,400
We got a car coming.

618
00:59:46,470 --> 00:59:47,800
- It's all right.
- Let's go.

619
00:59:47,870 --> 00:59:49,430
Shit!

620
00:59:49,500 --> 00:59:50,990
Come on.

621
00:59:51,070 --> 00:59:53,900
Let's go. Hurry!

622
00:59:56,310 --> 00:59:58,780
Put her in the back.

623
00:59:58,850 --> 01:00:00,970
All right, get in, lie low.

624
01:00:08,920 --> 01:00:11,910
- Hey, Sean, it's them.
- It could be anybody.

625
01:00:13,430 --> 01:00:15,660
Yeah, but if it's them,
we can't make a stand here.

626
01:00:15,730 --> 01:00:17,660
We gotta get to the mission.

627
01:00:23,840 --> 01:00:25,270
- Shit.
- It's them.

628
01:00:25,340 --> 01:00:27,430
They've seen us.

629
01:00:27,510 --> 01:00:29,170
Start the car.

630
01:00:34,280 --> 01:00:37,220
- Come on! Not now!
- What's going on?

631
01:00:37,280 --> 01:00:40,310
- It's not going into gear.
- Man, we gotta get out.

632
01:00:40,390 --> 01:00:42,720
- Come on!
- They're coming. Go!

633
01:00:42,790 --> 01:00:45,380
Yank it! Come on!

634
01:00:45,460 --> 01:00:47,520
Go! Come on!

635
01:00:47,590 --> 01:00:50,290
Go, go, go!

636
01:00:54,570 --> 01:00:56,000
Sean, come on! Let's go!

637
01:00:56,070 --> 01:00:58,400
Take a fucking left!
Let's go!

638
01:01:00,170 --> 01:01:02,540
No! Left!

639
01:01:10,820 --> 01:01:14,690
- What the hell is he doing?
- Whoo! Go! Go!

640
01:01:16,060 --> 01:01:19,290
- Sean, what are you doing?
- Playing a little chicken.

641
01:01:20,490 --> 01:01:22,020
Come on, you pussies!

642
01:01:31,440 --> 01:01:33,410
Want to play chicken
with me, boy?

643
01:01:36,240 --> 01:01:37,730
Come on.

644
01:01:39,510 --> 01:01:41,110
Don't turn that wheel.

645
01:01:41,180 --> 01:01:42,770
Rock and roll!

646
01:01:53,430 --> 01:01:54,950
Damn it!

647
01:01:59,030 --> 01:02:00,400
Motherfucker.

648
01:02:08,540 --> 01:02:10,810
- They're still on us.
- These guys don't give up.

649
01:02:15,950 --> 01:02:17,810
We gotta make it to the mission.

650
01:02:46,650 --> 01:02:48,140
What the hell is this?

651
01:02:51,350 --> 01:02:53,410
You gotta be
fucking kidding me.

652
01:03:02,100 --> 01:03:04,030
You gotta make a decision.

653
01:03:05,700 --> 01:03:07,460
We're going for it.

654
01:03:35,160 --> 01:03:37,650
How the hell did you know
you were gonna get through there?

655
01:03:37,730 --> 01:03:39,160
I didn't.

656
01:03:41,170 --> 01:03:43,730
Let's get the fuck out of here.

657
01:04:10,500 --> 01:04:14,060
- How much farther is it to the mission?
- About ten miles.

658
01:04:14,130 --> 01:04:17,230
We don't have enough gas
to make it there.

659
01:04:20,340 --> 01:04:21,570
Looks deserted, man.

660
01:04:29,020 --> 01:04:31,810
- It's all locked up.
- Shit.

661
01:04:33,520 --> 01:04:35,390
We gotta get her inside.

662
01:04:35,460 --> 01:04:38,690
The pills are working on her,
but she can barely walk.

663
01:04:38,760 --> 01:04:41,920
Once she gets some sleep,
she'll be okay.

664
01:04:44,260 --> 01:04:45,700
Nothing?

665
01:04:51,370 --> 01:04:53,000
Damn it!

666
01:04:56,380 --> 01:04:58,640
Buster.

667
01:04:58,710 --> 01:05:01,440
Get your butts outta here!

668
01:05:01,520 --> 01:05:03,640
Believe me, ma'am,
we would love to.

669
01:05:03,720 --> 01:05:06,150
But we're almost out of gas.

670
01:05:06,220 --> 01:05:08,920
We're not looking for a handout,
all right? We'll buy it.

671
01:05:08,990 --> 01:05:12,220
- Ain't got any to sell.
- Could we use your phone?

672
01:05:12,290 --> 01:05:14,230
Ain't got one.

673
01:05:15,330 --> 01:05:16,660
Jesus!

674
01:05:18,370 --> 01:05:21,770
Listen to me.
We are in a lot of trouble.

675
01:05:21,840 --> 01:05:24,500
This girl here is really sick.

676
01:05:24,570 --> 01:05:26,000
Please.

677
01:05:32,580 --> 01:05:34,980
You better get her on in here.

678
01:05:36,920 --> 01:05:39,910
- Why would they go this way?
- Just drive.

679
01:05:39,990 --> 01:05:42,980
What the fuck are we doing, anyway?
Let'em go. We got bigger problems.

680
01:05:43,060 --> 01:05:45,960
Who's gonna day drive for us?

681
01:06:26,970 --> 01:06:27,990
You're gonna turn.

682
01:06:30,040 --> 01:06:32,000
You gotta take drugs
to slow the virus.

683
01:06:50,320 --> 01:06:53,260
Do you want something
to eat, my man?

684
01:06:55,130 --> 01:06:58,000
- What's wrong?
- I don't feel so good.

685
01:07:00,200 --> 01:07:01,720
I feel like I did before.

686
01:07:01,800 --> 01:07:07,100
- I need some more of those drugs.
- The cocktail doesn't always work.

687
01:07:11,810 --> 01:07:13,750
She's resting now.

688
01:07:16,950 --> 01:07:18,880
Seems to be okay.

689
01:07:22,360 --> 01:07:24,550
Doesn't say much, does she?

690
01:07:24,620 --> 01:07:26,620
There's gotta be someplace
we can get her some help.

691
01:07:26,690 --> 01:07:30,790
Fort Stockton's the closest,
and it's over a hundred miles.

692
01:07:31,870 --> 01:07:33,460
Fuck.

693
01:07:33,530 --> 01:07:37,730
What's wrong with that little gal
that you're traveling with?

694
01:07:37,800 --> 01:07:40,860
- We don't know.
- She was hitchhiking.

695
01:07:40,940 --> 01:07:42,460
She was like that
when we picked her up.

696
01:07:42,540 --> 01:07:44,740
She didn't say who she was?

697
01:07:44,810 --> 01:07:47,410
She hasn't said a damned word
since we gave her a ride.

698
01:07:47,480 --> 01:07:49,970
I think maybe...

699
01:07:51,850 --> 01:07:55,290
you should take a look at this.

700
01:08:50,340 --> 01:08:52,310
You've lost the connection,
haven't you?

701
01:08:56,880 --> 01:09:00,180
I don't know why
we keep chasing that little bitch.

702
01:09:01,790 --> 01:09:03,810
It's unfinished business.

703
01:09:09,100 --> 01:09:10,320
Kill her.

704
01:09:19,940 --> 01:09:25,470
He left her to kill me.
I don't know why she didn't.

705
01:09:29,250 --> 01:09:34,190
When she pointed the gun at me,
I couldn't breathe.

706
01:09:36,360 --> 01:09:38,550
I couldn't even move.

707
01:09:39,730 --> 01:09:41,790
But I think she was scared...

708
01:09:41,860 --> 01:09:45,520
because she just stood there.

709
01:09:47,070 --> 01:09:49,800
She had the strangest look
in her eyes.

710
01:09:51,340 --> 01:09:54,600
After that,
I don't remember much at all.

711
01:10:00,380 --> 01:10:01,610
What's with the dog?

712
01:10:02,980 --> 01:10:06,150
Just stay put.
Probably just a coyote.

713
01:10:14,460 --> 01:10:15,890
Buster.

714
01:10:30,910 --> 01:10:32,000
What was it?

715
01:10:33,350 --> 01:10:36,080
I don't know.
Buster ran off.

716
01:10:42,220 --> 01:10:44,380
Everybody down!
Get under the table!

717
01:10:44,460 --> 01:10:46,620
Hurry up!
Go, go! Get down!

718
01:11:35,170 --> 01:11:37,730
Where's your shotgun?

719
01:11:37,810 --> 01:11:42,180
It's by the side door. There's
extra shells in the refrigerator.

720
01:12:30,900 --> 01:12:34,830
- What's with those tombstones?
- It's an old Spanish graveyard.

721
01:12:34,900 --> 01:12:37,030
That's why the highway
wasn't put through here.

722
01:12:37,100 --> 01:12:39,040
They couldn't dig it up.

723
01:12:39,110 --> 01:12:41,900
Your house is actually built
on a graveyard?

724
01:12:44,540 --> 01:12:46,380
Are you thinking what I'm thinking?

725
01:12:46,450 --> 01:12:48,880
This place is blessed, baby.

726
01:12:51,180 --> 01:12:52,310
Sean, watch out!

727
01:12:58,160 --> 01:13:00,490
- Come on!
- Stop!

728
01:13:19,280 --> 01:13:21,510
Let's go upstairs.

729
01:13:45,340 --> 01:13:47,310
Let's get this over with.

730
01:14:36,990 --> 01:14:39,820
Come to Daddy, boys!

731
01:15:16,630 --> 01:15:19,290
Are you in there, piggies?

732
01:15:20,270 --> 01:15:22,460
Yum, yum, yum.
Eat'em up.

733
01:16:15,490 --> 01:16:17,220
Now that's a bitch!

734
01:16:30,940 --> 01:16:32,870
I got the motherfucker!

735
01:16:34,510 --> 01:16:36,810
Make sure and take his head off.

736
01:16:48,220 --> 01:16:51,920
Nick, I don't see...

737
01:17:05,670 --> 01:17:09,330
Make your stand, punk.
Let's see what you got.

738
01:17:49,180 --> 01:17:51,550
Not much left, huh?

739
01:17:52,650 --> 01:17:54,680
Kill me.

740
01:18:02,330 --> 01:18:05,960
Kill you?
Who said anything about killing?

741
01:18:06,030 --> 01:18:08,360
You're gonna be my new day driver.

742
01:18:08,430 --> 01:18:12,300
At least until you turn, and then
I don't give a shit what you do.

743
01:18:14,510 --> 01:18:17,810
Get the car
and bring it around.

744
01:18:30,690 --> 01:18:33,920
And if you fuck with me,
I'll kill your little blonde friend...

745
01:18:33,990 --> 01:18:36,590
in the blink of an eye.

746
01:18:46,440 --> 01:18:50,030
It's just the beast under your bed

747
01:18:50,110 --> 01:18:53,240
In your closet, in your head

748
01:18:53,380 --> 01:18:56,180
Exit light

749
01:18:56,250 --> 01:18:59,310
Enter night

750
01:19:01,590 --> 01:19:04,350
You're off to never-never land.

751
01:19:12,670 --> 01:19:16,620
Got an opening for a new girlfriend.
What do you say?

752
01:19:16,700 --> 01:19:20,660
- Fuck you!
- Ooh, attitude.

753
01:19:20,740 --> 01:19:25,200
I like that in a girl.
Now move away from the old witch.

754
01:19:27,250 --> 01:19:32,620
Look, darling, I'm gonna waste her
sure as the sun shines.

755
01:19:32,690 --> 01:19:34,950
You could stay with her and die...

756
01:19:35,020 --> 01:19:39,320
or you can come with me
and I'll let you live.

757
01:19:55,470 --> 01:19:57,670
It's time to make your stand, punk.

758
01:19:58,810 --> 01:20:00,800
Let's see what you've got.

759
01:20:35,680 --> 01:20:37,080
No! Come on!

760
01:20:37,150 --> 01:20:39,740
Out of gas, are we?

761
01:20:48,330 --> 01:20:54,030
Didn't I fucking tell you
to do something?

762
01:21:12,720 --> 01:21:14,410
You know what?

763
01:21:15,490 --> 01:21:17,980
Why don't you drive
your own fucking car!

764
01:22:48,250 --> 01:22:52,880
- How do you feel?
- Good. You?

765
01:22:52,950 --> 01:22:55,180
Going home today.

766
01:22:55,250 --> 01:22:58,690
Actually, not home.
My aunt and uncle's place in Phoenix.

767
01:23:00,290 --> 01:23:03,920
Well, they said I could probably
go home tomorrow.

768
01:23:04,000 --> 01:23:06,230
Might still make
my sister's wedding.

769
01:23:06,300 --> 01:23:09,100
I saw Ina this morning.

770
01:23:10,440 --> 01:23:13,270
She's okay, but
she doesn't remember what happened.

771
01:23:14,440 --> 01:23:17,000
Yeah. Nobody suspects a thing.

772
01:23:17,080 --> 01:23:19,200
Just a couple of bad guys
burned up in a fire.

773
01:23:19,280 --> 01:23:23,110
- Probably better that way, huh?
- Yeah.

774
01:23:23,180 --> 01:23:27,280
- No one would believe it.
- Yeah, probably not.

775
01:23:30,920 --> 01:23:33,860
Well, I gotta go.

776
01:23:35,260 --> 01:23:38,090
I just wanted to thank you
for everything.

777
01:23:38,160 --> 01:23:39,100
Yeah.

778
01:24:11,560 --> 01:24:13,930
What's up?
Where's the guy that was here?

779
01:24:14,000 --> 01:24:16,630
He checked out, I guess.

780
01:24:16,700 --> 01:24:18,400
He left this for you.

781
01:24:26,950 --> 01:24:29,740
By the time you read this,
I'll be on the road again.

782
01:24:29,820 --> 01:24:33,180
Yours and Megan's fight is over, :
mine ain't.

783
01:24:33,250 --> 01:24:35,220
It turns out
he wasn't the one I was looking for.

784
01:24:35,290 --> 01:24:37,480
Mine's still out there somewhere.

785
01:24:40,990 --> 01:24:44,550
But the way I figure it,
if I can find one, I can find another.

786
01:24:44,630 --> 01:24:48,260
They might be bad motherfuckers,
but we're not talking brain surgeons.

787
01:24:48,330 --> 01:24:51,460
So, anyways, thanks.
It was cool hanging with you.

788
01:24:51,540 --> 01:24:54,100
Maybe I'll see you again sometime.

789
01:25:25,600 --> 01:25:28,940
- Nice ride, man.
- Had you going for a minute, didn't I?

790
01:25:29,010 --> 01:25:32,070
- I took it from an old friend.
- Yeah, right.

791
01:25:44,120 --> 01:25:46,460
How in the hell did you find me?

792
01:25:46,530 --> 01:25:47,960
Well...

793
01:25:49,830 --> 01:25:52,730
I drove just about
every damned road...

794
01:25:52,800 --> 01:25:56,060
from Nevada to Kansas,
from Mexico to Montana...

795
01:25:56,140 --> 01:25:58,300
for about three months.

796
01:25:58,370 --> 01:26:01,170
Then I wised up
and started doing what you do.

797
01:26:01,240 --> 01:26:03,970
I checked the news,
read the papers.

798
01:26:04,040 --> 01:26:07,410
You're right.
They do hide the killings.

799
01:26:07,480 --> 01:26:10,210
But if you look hard enough,
you can find them.

800
01:26:10,280 --> 01:26:11,480
Thanks.

801
01:26:14,350 --> 01:26:16,650
He's been a bad boy, Nick.

802
01:26:16,720 --> 01:26:20,020
And busy.
Busier than the last one.

803
01:26:21,230 --> 01:26:23,160
The way I figure it,
he's going to Denver.

804
01:26:23,230 --> 01:26:25,250
This guy moves fast,
so he's not gonna stay there long.

805
01:26:25,330 --> 01:26:28,420
You don't have to do this.
You know that.

806
01:26:28,500 --> 01:26:30,200
Yeah, I do.

807
01:26:42,210 --> 01:26:45,710
So tell me, was that woman
really pissed about her Mercedes?

808
01:26:45,780 --> 01:26:47,220
Oh, yeah.


